# Code owners for specifica.
#
# Owners are requested automatically on any PR touching a matching path.
# Last match wins, so the specific rules below override the catch-all.
#
# THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL TWO THINGS ARE DONE — neither reports an error
# when missing:
#
#   1. @cogniumhq/coreteam must have WRITE access to this repository.
#      GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries naming a team without
#      write access. At time of writing `GET /repos/cogniumhq/specifica/teams`
#      returns [] — no team has been granted access to this repo.
#   2. `main` is NOT a protected branch here (`protected: false`), so changes
#      can be pushed straight to it without a pull request at all. Code owners
#      are only consulted on PRs; branch protection with "Require review from
#      Code Owners" has to be enabled for this file to gate anything.
#
# See cogniumhq/cognium-dev#442.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @cogniumhq/coreteam

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain. @specifica/format and @specifica/store are published to npm
# (private: false), so a change to a manifest or the lockfile can introduce a
# malicious dependency into anything that installs them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/package.json                       @cogniumhq/coreteam
/package-lock.json                  @cogniumhq/coreteam
/packages/*/package.json            @cogniumhq/coreteam

# This repo has no workflows today. The rule is deliberate rather than dead:
# what it guards is the *creation* of one, which is the point at which CI
# gains the ability to execute arbitrary code and publish packages.
/.github/                           @cogniumhq/coreteam
